\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One normal direction}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{In dimension #{1} each transverse layer has one site.
Both transverse sums in the [normal transfer](fdip-01BF)
are empty. Put #{b=1-a_sM}. For #{b\ne0} the step sends
#{(u,v)} to #{(b^{-1}u,bv)}. It is strictly positive for
#{b>0} and strictly negative for #{b<0}. At #{b=0}, specifying
zero input leaves the new #{W_+} value arbitrary.}
